              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Federal Petitioners, section\u202f253(a) preempts state laws that prohibit or have the effect of prohibiting any entity from providing telecommunications services."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Feldman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0003-0002",
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Feldman, congress contemplated giving states some leeway, but it never intended to intrude on state sovereignty in the way the Eighth Circuit held."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Federal Petitioners (Mr. Feldman)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner Nixon",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 16,
                "start": 16
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner Nixon, the Eighth Circuit interprets \u201centity\u201d to include political subdivisions of the states, which would give Missouri\u2019s political subdivisions authority that the state itself has withheld."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Nixon (Mr. Molteni)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "David A. Strauss",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to David A. Strauss, gregory\u202fv.\u202fAshcroft applies when statutory language is ambiguous, but the language of \u00a7253(a) \u2013 \u201cany entity\u201d \u2013 is not ambiguous."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "David A. Strauss",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            },
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            },
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Congress intended \u201cany entity\u201d to include municipal corporations, treating them as competitors in the telecommunications market."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Strauss",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0cbead4345c3f09ffab1f492919f31e67d39147515eb0288eef7e75a8d6210f1",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0cbead4345c3-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Strauss, the State cannot repeal the statute unless it is part of a competitively neutral reorganization of local government."
        }
